de'i li 20 pi'e 06 pi'e 2009 la'o fy. David Gowers .fy. cusku zoi  
skamyxatra.
 > I was writing about a numeric encoding system and eventually wrote  
this:
 >
 > li no ga'o bi'o ga'o vo nosomu pi sososomupapazepabizemu cu nacyja'e
 > sekai le papamei jetka'usatci va'i se'i li pa fi'u renovobi
 >
 > in English:
 >   numeric-result is in range [0 .. 4095.99951171875].
 >    with-property 11 bit-precision - in other words 1 / 2048
...
 > Is this appropriate? 'and in other words 1/2048' seems still a bit  
odd.
 > I really just want to specify '11 bit-precision, in other words
 > 1/2048'; is that un-lojbanic or am I just ignorant ? :)
.skamyxatra

"{va'i}" and "{se'i}" both belong to {selma'o} UI, so they act as  
attitudinals/indicators and do not start new structures; thus, "{li pa  
fi'u renovobi}" simply fills the x2 place of "{nacyja'e}."  I think  
the suggested way to say what you're trying to say is with a  
parenthetical: "... {sekai le papamei jetka'usatci to va'i se'i li pa  
fi'u renovobi toi}."

mu'omi'e .kamymecraijun.

